id: pm-hv1x1x
title: "MCP server surface and cache contracts: deterministic tools, prompts, resources, JSON Schema 2020-12, ttlMs, cacheScope, and change coherence"
description: "Bring every pm MCP list/read/call surface onto the 2026-07-28 schema and caching contract with deterministic ordering, broad JSON Schema support, safe references, and coherent invalidation."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[8]: "area:mcp",caching,determinism,json-schema,prompts,resources,token-efficiency,tools
created_at: "2026-08-25T05:09:49.804Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-25T05:09:49.804Z"
deadline: "2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 780
acceptance_criteria: "Every cacheable result includes validated ttlMs and cacheScope with documented freshness and privacy semantics; Tool listing is deterministic and cache invalidation composes correctly with listChanged and subscriptions/listen; JSON Schema 2020-12 references and composition keywords work within explicit recursion, size, and work bounds; structuredContent accepts every JSON value and schema-validation refusals are actionable and token-bounded; Resource-not-found uses Invalid Params and never leaks resource existence outside caller authority; SDK, MCP, docs, generated schemas, golden snapshots, and packed artifacts prove one shared contract"
goal: Complete cacheable deterministic server features
objective: "Make tool, prompt, resource, template, and read results conformant, bounded, cache-safe, and generated from shared SDK contracts"
value: "Clients spend fewer tokens and requests while preserving exact freshness, privacy, and schema semantics"
why_now: "The new revision requires ttlMs and cacheScope on cacheable results, deterministic tool ordering, broader JSON Schema 2020-12 behavior, and different resource-not-found errors"
parent: pm-rs9vry
risk: high
confidence: high
